CM_ SG_ 938 Port_Open "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs and live: charge port door. Set to Open as soon as the door starts opening. Does not change when a charger is plugged in or charging.";
CM_ SG_ 1043 HAZARD_ON "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 1 while the hazard switch is on.";
CM_ SG_ 843 Headlight_Switch "Wrong on an EV6: steps through every value once a second whatever the switch position. The switch position is not on this bus; BCM_07_200ms has the lamp outputs.";
CM_ SG_ 550 Outdoor_Temperature "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: matches the dashboard outside temperature while the car displays Celsius; Not_Available (255) while it displays Fahrenheit, then ODOMETER Outdoor_Temperature_F has it.";
CM_ SG_ 551 Odometer "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: matches the dashboard odometer. Stays in km when the car displays miles.";
CM_ SG_ 764 State_Of_Charge "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs and live: matches the dashboard SOC.";
CM_ BO_ 412 "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: only seen on one L2 charger.";
CM_ SG_ 412 Cand_AC_Current_19C "Candidate: reads 11.9-12.0 A while charging on a 240 V 15 A circuit (2.6-2.7 kW) and 0 on DC or idle. Reads 12.3-12.4 A from plug-in until charging starts, so maybe the charger's advertised limit then. 0x30D byte 5 carries the same values.";
CM_ SG_ 412 Cand_19C_16 "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: ramps from 0 to 210 in steps of 20 per frame when L2 charging starts and holds 210 until it stops, on every L2 log (one charger). Maybe the AC voltage, but 210 V x 11.9 A = 2.5 kW, not the 2.7 kW the car shows; Car Scanner doesn't show the AC voltage to check it.";
CM_ SG_ 413 Charger_Type "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: charger type. The car tries DC first, so it reads DC for the first seconds on an AC charger, then None, then AC about 7 s after plug-in.";
CM_ SG_ 413 DC_Sequence_Stage "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: DC charging sequence. 1 plugged in, 2 and 3 talking to the charger, 4 ready, 5 starting, 6 charging, 8 to 11 ending. An AC charger goes from 1 straight to 9 to 11 while the car gives up on DC; stages 2 to 6 mean the charger really is DC.";
CM_ SG_ 780 Proximity_Voltage "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: charge inlet proximity voltage. About 4.4 V unplugged, 1.5 V plugged in and latched, 2.7 V while the plug release button is pressed. AC and DC.";
CM_ SG_ 780 Plug_Connected "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 1 while a charging cable is plugged in, AC or DC. Changes right at plug-in and unplug.";
CM_ SG_ 806 AC_Charger "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 1 once the car has recognised an AC charger, about 7 s after plug-in. Never set on DC.";
CM_ SG_ 806 Charging "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 1 while energy flows into the battery, AC or DC.";
CM_ SG_ 764 Battery_Current "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: high-voltage battery current, positive when discharging. Times Battery_Voltage it matches CHARGING_POWER on DC (within 1 kW) and gives 2.2 kW into the battery on a 2.6-2.7 kW L2 charger. Peaks at +198 A on a hard launch and -57 A in regen.";
CM_ SG_ 567 Battery_Voltage "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: high-voltage battery voltage. About 702 V at rest at 42% SOC, rises to 760 V while DC charging and sags under load.";
CM_ SG_ 54 Ready "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 1 while the car is ready to drive, in any gear; 0 when off, in accessory or on but not ready, and while charging with the car off. Drops when a DC charger is plugged in while ready, as the cluster does. Bit 30 is set with it, and bits 26 and 30 rise a few hundred ms before it at start-up.";
CM_ SG_ 54 Gear "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: selected gear, follows every shift in log_09 within about a second, including the brief Neutral between Drive and Reverse. Reads 0 (Park) with the car off, asleep or charging. Bit 36 next to it is cleared while the high-voltage system is live: ready, or charging. Undefined message 0x039 byte 0 carries the same values but reads 9 while the car is off or charging.";
CM_ SG_ 54 Drive_Mode "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: active drive mode, changes as the mode button is pressed. Reads 0 (Eco) with the car off. Snow reads 5 (the Normal bits plus bit 60).";
CM_ SG_ 695 Range "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: range shown on the cluster, for the active drive mode only; the other modes are not sent. Stays in km when the car displays miles. Bit 11 of the message blips for about 2 s when a navigation route starts or stops.";
CM_ BO_ 818 "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: the car's estimate for a DC fast charge, always whole minutes, sent all the time (also driving and while AC charging); 0 with the car off. Matches the cluster while DC charging. For the charge in progress use CHARGING_TIME.";
CM_ SG_ 818 Charge_Time_To_Limit "Seconds for a DC fast charge to the DC limit (100% in all logs, so it may be to 100%).";
CM_ SG_ 818 Charge_Time_To_80 "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: seconds for a DC fast charge to 80%, as the cluster shows next to the time to the limit while DC charging.";
CM_ SG_ 1144 DRIVE_MODE "Wrong on an EV6: barely sent and the values make no sense. Use DRIVE_MODE_STATUS Drive_Mode.";
CM_ SG_ 428 Speed_kph "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with timed notes: speed in km/h, also while the car displays miles (log_32: 17-18 where the cluster showed 10 mph | 17 km/h), like the range and odometer. CLUSTER_DISPLAY_UNITS Display_Speed has it in the display unit.";
CM_ SG_ 795 Steering_Wheel_Heating_State "Wrong on an EV6: toggles about once a second whatever the heater does. Use ICU_08_200ms HSWS_SysWrngSta_ICU.";
CM_ SG_ 795 Climate_AC_State "Not the A/C state: 0 at a time the A/C was on, follows the A/C button but also changes with Auto and Heat. Use DATC_05_200ms DATC_AcDis.";
CM_ SG_ 795 Climate_Fan_Speed "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: blower level plus one (manual levels 1 to 8 read 2 to 9), 0 with the climate off; follows the blower in Auto.";
CM_ SG_ 795 Climate_Airflow_Direction "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs.";
CM_ SG_ 795 Climate_Recirculation_State "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: recirculation on or off.";
CM_ SG_ 896 Driver_Temp_C "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: driver target temperature.";
CM_ SG_ 896 Passenger_Temp_C "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: passenger target temperature; OFF while Driver only is on.";
CM_ SG_ 896 Driver_Temp_F "Not Fahrenheit on a car set to Celsius: repeats the Driver_Temp_C steps. Not checked in Fahrenheit.";
CM_ SG_ 896 Passenger_Temp_F "Not Fahrenheit on a car set to Celsius: repeats the Passenger_Temp_C steps. Not checked in Fahrenheit.";
CM_ SG_ 593 Rear_Defrost_State "Wrong on an EV6: toggles every few seconds whatever the rear defroster does. No rear defroster state on this bus (nothing changed with it on for 27 s).";
CM_ SG_ 685 Battery_Precond_State "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: battery preconditioning. Preparing at the request; On when the battery heater switches on (about 60 s later, varies), which is when the cluster shows the battery icon. 2 while the car is off, asleep or charging.";
CM_ SG_ 1174 Driver_Seat_Heating_Oper "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: driver seat heating level. 3 to 5 may be ventilation (not checked).";
CM_ SG_ 1141 Passenger_Seat_Heating_Oper "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: passenger seat heating level. 3 to 5 may be ventilation (not checked).";
CM_ SG_ 1261 Precond_Request "Not an on/off request: 0x1F with bytes 5-6 at FF FF when no route is set, and route data (e.g. 08 48 00) when navigating to a DC charger, about 6 s before preconditioning starts. Probably route information for the BMU; the old value table (31 = On, 0 = Off) was backwards. wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition) overwrites bytes 5-7 with 10 A0 00 while it keeps preconditioning on.";
CM_ SG_ 605 Cand_Heater_Power_25D "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: 45-46 while the battery heater runs during preconditioning, matching the extra ~4.5 kW drawn from the battery, so probably 0.1 kW steps; 0 otherwise. Only seen in summer, so cabin heating may use it too.";
CM_ SG_ 337 AC_Charge_Limit "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with timed notes: AC charge limit set in the head unit, applied about 3 s after the change. 0x1F9 bytes 2-3 carry the same pair.";
CM_ SG_ 337 DC_Charge_Limit "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with timed notes: DC charge limit set in the head unit.";
CM_ SG_ 435 Cabin_Temperature "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with a thermometer next to the cabin sensor: about 1 C above it (10 to 20 C while heating); drops with the climate off.";
CM_ SG_ 504 Charging_Time_To_Limit "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with timed notes: minutes to the charge limit for the charge in progress, AC and DC, as the cluster shows; 0 when not charging. Byte 6 was only set once (420 min).";
CM_ SG_ 551 Outdoor_Temperature_F "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: outside temperature while the car displays Fahrenheit (44.5 F for 45 F shown, 7 C); 255 while it displays Celsius.";
CM_ SG_ 898 DATC_TempDispUnitSta "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with timed notes: temperature display unit.";
CM_ BO_ 162 "Wheel mapping (FL, FR, RL, RR) is assumed and requires live verification.";
CM_ SG_ 764 Battery_Min_Temperature "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs and Car Scanner: lowest battery module temperature, 12 C where Car Scanner showed 12 C (log_31); rises from 26 to 29 C during a DC fast charge (log_21). Never below 8 C in the logs, so the sign is assumed. BATTERY_TEMPERATURES_152 byte 0 carries the same value.";
CM_ SG_ 764 Battery_Max_Temperature "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs and Car Scanner: highest battery module temperature, 13 C where Car Scanner showed 13 C (log_31); rises from 28 to 31 C during a DC fast charge (log_21), always at or above Battery_Min_Temperature. CHARGE_LIMITS byte 7 carries the same value.";
CM_ SG_ 764 Aux_Battery_Voltage "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs and Car Scanner: 12 V battery voltage. 13.5-14.3 V while the car is on or charging (DC-DC converter running), falls to about 12.1 V within seconds of switching off and climbs back when charging starts (log_31). Car Scanner read 13.9 V at the OBD port when this read 13.6 V. Reads 0 for one frame while the car switches off.";
CM_ SG_ 337 Battery_Max_Temperature_Copy "Checked on an EV6 against CAN logs: same value as BATTERY_INFO_764 Battery_Max_Temperature, changing at the same moments in log_21.";
CM_ BO_ 338 "Checked on an EV6 against CAN logs: battery temperatures, changing slowly during a DC fast charge (log_21).";
CM_ SG_ 338 Battery_Min_Temperature_Copy "Checked on an EV6 against CAN logs: same value as BATTERY_INFO_764 Battery_Min_Temperature.";
CM_ SG_ 338 Cand_Battery_Temp_152_8 "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: between the battery minimum and maximum temperatures (13 C at 12/13 C in log_31, 27-30 C during a DC charge in log_21). Maybe a coolant or average temperature; Car Scanner showed 12 C coolant, which doesn't tell it apart. wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition) reads it as the battery maximum, which the EV6 logs contradict.";
CM_ SG_ 338 Cand_Battery_Temp_152_16 "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: like Cand_Battery_Temp_152_8 (12 C in log_31, 27-30 C in log_21).";
CM_ SG_ 427 Distance_Unit "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with timed notes: distance display unit, set when switching to miles and cleared when switching back to km (log_30 at 6:52 and 7:11).";
CM_ SG_ 427 Display_Speed "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with timed notes: speed in the display unit, 0.5 steps. In km/h it is twice CLUSTER_INFO_428 Speed_kph (65 km/h reads 130); in miles it matched the seven mph readings in log_32. Byte 7 has always been 0, but no log goes above 119 km/h, so the 16-bit width is assumed: the car goes faster than the 127.5 that byte 6 alone can hold.";
CM_ BO_ 738 "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with a video of the cluster (log_32): regenerative braking level and Auto.";
CM_ SG_ 738 Regen_Auto "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with a video of the cluster: 1 while the paddles are in Auto regen (log_32 from 1:28 to 1:52), 0 for fixed levels and i-Pedal.";
CM_ SG_ 738 Regen_Level "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with a video of the cluster: regen strength, 0 to 3 for the paddle levels and 4 for the maximum (i-Pedal, or the maximum without i-Pedal). In Auto it moves smoothly between them (0.1, 0.8, 1.9 seen) and the cluster numbers the steps one higher (Auto level 1 to 5). Not_Available with the car off and while smart cruise drives the car. Resets to 3 in Park and Reverse.";
CM_ SG_ 739 I_Pedal "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with a video of the cluster: 1 in i-Pedal, 0 at fixed levels, in Auto and at the maximum level without i-Pedal (log_32 1:52 to 1:56). Keeps its last value with the car off.";
CM_ BO_ 929 "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with the cluster's tire screen: tire pressures in whole psi, with the cluster set to psi; it can also show kPa, which was never captured and may change these bytes. Not_Available until the sensors report, a minute or two into a drive. Front left (log_33, deflated to 32 psi) and rear left (log_34, 36 psi) are confirmed; front right and rear right are assumed from the usual order, as neither was ever set apart. Bytes 0-1 hold a 14-bit CRC.";
CM_ SG_ 929 Tire_Pressure_FL "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with the cluster's tire screen: front left (dropped from 35 to 32 psi when only that tire was deflated, log_33).";
CM_ SG_ 929 Tire_Pressure_FR "Assumed front right from the usual wheel order; never set apart from the others.";
CM_ SG_ 929 Tire_Pressure_RL "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs with the cluster's tire screen: rear left (toggled 35/36 psi with the cluster's rear left, log_34).";
CM_ SG_ 929 Tire_Pressure_RR "Assumed rear right from the usual wheel order; never set apart from the others.";
CM_ BO_ 1264 "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: the head unit clock, local time with the date, sent every 250 ms and stepping once a second. Matches the date of all 53 captures (June to October) and the time each of log_01 to log_34 was saved (EDT). Reads all ones for the first frames after the car wakes up. Byte 0 (0x8A) and bit 38 (set) never changed; they may hold the 12/24 h or daylight saving settings, never changed in a capture.";
CM_ SG_ 1264 Hours "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 0-23 whatever the clock format shown (only 24 h was captured).";
CM_ SG_ 1264 Year "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 26 for 2026.";
CM_ BO_ 1259 "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: the same local time as LOCAL_TIME with the day of the week instead of the date, sent every 200 ms and stepping once a second, at most a second off LOCAL_TIME.";
CM_ SG_ 1259 Weekday "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: one bit per day, in the order of the departure-day bits of HU_EV_P_1263 (Sunday in bit 0 up to Monday in bit 6). Sunday, Saturday, Friday and Monday were captured; Tuesday to Thursday follow from that order.";
CM_ SG_ 1259 NEW_SIGNAL_3 "Unverified opendbc signal";
CM_ BO_ 1230 "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: head unit media status, sent once a second. Reads FE C3 then all FF while the car is off. Frames with bytes 4-5 at 28 04 or other odd values come in between around track changes; ignore them. The track text itself goes out over ISO-TP, one CAN ID per source as listed by wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition): Android Auto on 0x6D2 (UTF-16LE title only, no flow control; seen in every log with music), Bluetooth 0x6D4, CarPlay 0x6D6, radio 0x6DC, USB 0x6EA, apps 0x6E0.";
CM_ SG_ 1230 Media_Source "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: Android Auto (0xDE) in every log with music, Off (0x14) in the captures without Bluetooth or Android Auto, and switching from Off to Android Auto when the phone connected (log_11). The other values come from wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition): 0x10/0x11 Bluetooth, 0x22-0x23 and 0x42-0x49 radio, 0xC4-0xCA USB, 0xDC/0xDD CarPlay.";
CM_ SG_ 1230 Media_Popup "Unverified: always 0x01 while the head unit is on in the logs. wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition) writes 0x11 for three frames to make the cluster pop up the track text it then sends over ISO-TP.";
CM_ SG_ 1230 Track_Seconds "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: playback position of the current track, back to 0 at each Android Auto title change on 0x6D2 and counting once a second. Counts 0-251, then Track_Seconds_High goes up by one (log_20, 4:12 into a track): position = Track_Seconds_High x 252 + Track_Seconds.";
CM_ SG_ 1230 Track_Seconds_High "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: see Track_Seconds. Only 0 and 1 seen (no track longer than about 8 min was played).";
CM_ BO_ 56 "Checked on an EV6 against CAN logs: power mode, the same state wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition) reads READY from. To investigate: it may be the high-voltage contactor or ICCU state rather than a plain power mode (3 looks like a precharge before Ready, 6 has the car awake for charging or a remote command), and byte 1 changes with each value (01/05 at 2, 0B/0C at 3, 00 at 4, 8x at 6). Not told apart yet from captures of remote commands, the 12 V top-up while asleep (orange ICCU light on the charge port) and V2L, ideally with Car Scanner showing the BMS relay status.";
CM_ SG_ 56 Power_Mode "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 4 exactly while DRIVE_MODE_STATUS Ready is set (log_09, log_30), 1 when off. Candidate meanings for the rest: 2 on without Ready, 3 for a fraction of a second while switching to Ready, 6 awake while plugged in or for a remote command.";
CM_ BO_ 1256 "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: the route summary the cluster shows during built-in navigation (the destination name goes over ISO-TP on 0x6E7, prefixed with 0xF4). All FF except byte 3 without a route; Android Auto navigation does not use it.";
CM_ SG_ 1256 Distance_Unit "From wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition), which writes this message to show a countdown on the cluster; consistent with the EV6 logs (km in every route). Shown together with Distance_Tenths only in km or mi and below 100.";
CM_ SG_ 1256 Distance_Tenths "Checked on an EV6 against CAN logs: tenths of Distance (7.9, 5.2 and 9.3 km for the three routes in the logs).";
CM_ SG_ 1256 ETA_Hours "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: hour of the estimated arrival time, local time. 23:24 for a route set at 23:12:49 (log_30); while parked it moves a minute later every minute, like the arrival time does.";
CM_ SG_ 1256 ETA_Minutes "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: minutes of the estimated arrival time, see ETA_Hours.";
CM_ SG_ 1256 Cand_Nav_Route_24 "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: without a route it steps by 3 as the car turns, like NAV_GUIDANCE Cand_Compass_Heading minus one; with a route 0x0B or 0x29, meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 1256 Distance "From wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition) (written to the cluster), consistent with the EV6 logs: whole part of the distance left, in Distance_Unit; 65535 hides the number.";
CM_ SG_ 1256 Destination_Flag "From wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition) (written to the cluster), consistent with the EV6 logs (Destination in every route): flag icon next to the distance.";
CM_ BO_ 1228 "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: the cluster turn-by-turn area. wicant-i-precondition (github.com/L1Z3/wicant-i-precondition) sets byte 0 to 0x02 to show the NAV_ROUTE distance.";
CM_ SG_ 1228 Cand_Guidance_Type "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: 0x08 without a route; 0x0D or 0x02 with one, probably the next maneuver. 0x09 for a moment while a route starts.";
CM_ SG_ 1228 Cand_Compass_Heading "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: without a route, 0-45 in steps of 3 following the car as it turns and wrapping from 45 to 0, so likely a 16-point compass heading; the direction of 0 is unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 418 "Checked on an EV6 against CAN logs: smart cruise control. Byte 0 also changes with it (0x14 engaged, 0x44 after a cancel), meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 418 Cruise_State "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 2 while cruise control is engaged, 0 otherwise (log_03, log_12, and the highway parts of log_20/22/24). 0x1A4 byte 1 leaves 07 at the same time.";
CM_ SG_ 418 Cruise_Set_Speed "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: the set speed. 70, then 60, then 50 km/h as set in log_12, stepping by 1 while the stalk is held; 50 in log_03. Stays at the last value after a cancel (Cruise_State 0) and reads 0 before cruise is first set. Only captured in km/h.";
CM_ BO_ 1255 "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: speed limit, probably the one the cluster shows. 0x1FB bytes 4 and 5 carry the same values times two.";
CM_ SG_ 1255 Cand_Displayed_Speed_Limit "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: 50, 70, 60, 30, 70, 50, 30 over log_12, changing with the road like HU_Navi_ISLW_PE Navi_ISLW_SpdLimit, but read 60 where the map said 30, so probably the camera-and-map limit the cluster shows. 0 when none is known. Not checked against the cluster.";
CM_ BO_ 1600 "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: lane guidance, also without a route. Each countdown starts when 0x680 sends an ISO-TP frame F1 <lane count> 00 <one code per lane> and ends when 0x680 sends all zeros (10 drive logs).";
CM_ SG_ 1600 Cand_Junction_Distance "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: distance to the next junction with lane guidance. Starts at 300 m or less, counts down in 10 m steps at the car's speed to 0-10, FF FF between junctions.";
CM_ SG_ 1600 Cand_Route_Active_640 "Candidate from EV6 CAN logs: 0x0A while a built-in navigation route is active, 0 otherwise.";
CM_ BO_ 763 "Requires more live testing. Behavior in charging logs is erratic.";
CM_ SG_ 1041 Passenger_Seatbelt_Fastened "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: front passenger seatbelt, follows all six buckles and unbuckles in log_05 within a second. The rear seatbelts and seat occupancy are not on this bus (log_05).";
CM_ SG_ 1041 Driver_Seatbelt_Fastened "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: driver seatbelt, follows all six buckles and unbuckles in log_05 within a second.";
CM_ SG_ 1041 Crc_Val "Unverified opendbc signal";
CM_ SG_ 1041 AlvCnt_Val "Unverified opendbc signal";
CM_ SG_ 938 Crc_Val "Unverified opendbc signal";
CM_ SG_ 938 AlvCnt_Val "Unverified opendbc signal";
CM_ SG_ 1044 Crc_Val "Unverified opendbc signal";
CM_ SG_ 1044 AlvCnt_Val "Unverified opendbc signal";
CM_ SG_ 1077 Crc_Val "Unverified opendbc signal";
CM_ SG_ 1077 AlvCnt_Val "Unverified opendbc signal";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Reverse_Lamp "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: 1 while in Reverse (reverse lights).";
CM_ SG_ 1042 Brake_Lamp "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: brake lights, 1 with the brake pedal pressed and also during strong regen without the pedal (log_15). Use ICU_08_200ms Brake_SwSta_ICU for the pedal itself. Was the 8-bit Brake_Pedal, which also caught the reverse lights.";
CM_ SG_ 100 Auto_Hold "Verified on an EV6 against CAN logs: Auto Hold switched On (48) or Off (4) with its button. The value while it is actively holding the car was not captured.";
CM_ SG_ 1077 Power_State "Checked on an EV6 against CAN logs: Car_on when on or ready, Car_Off when off or in accessory. Use BCM_02_200ms and DRIVE_MODE_STATUS Ready for the full power state.";
